  "mn31:0.2": "<p>Introduction</p><p><i>According to the Commentary, the events reported in this discourse follow on the events of a discourse in the Final Fifty of the Majjhima Nikāya, by which it obviously means <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn128'>MN 128.</a> There is a fair amount of overlap between this discourse and that, but as the Commentary notes, in that discourse the three monks mentioned here were still run-of-the-mill people, trying to find their way. After putting into practice the Buddha’s teaching given in that discourse, they all became arahants, a fact that is reported and celebrated here.</i></p><p>See also: <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn39'>MN 39–40</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn52.9'>SN 52:9</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn52.10'>SN 52:10</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an3.95'>AN 3:96</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an9.31'>AN 9:31–38</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/iti82'>Iti 82</a></p>",
